-- title:
--   An integral spanning set with jointly surjective residues
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ contain every unit reducing to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`) and with algebraically closed residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$. Write $F_M$ and $F_{M/p}$ for the base changes to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series, of the function fields at level $H$ and at level the image `infSubgroup` of $H$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Let $\theta$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of $F_M$, and $\alpha : F_{M/p} \to F_M$ an integral $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra map which is the identity on underlying Laurent series. Let `Psp` be a place specialisation datum for $p, M, H, A$ and `Rpd` a prolongation datum for `Psp` and $\theta$, consisting of two regular prolongations $R_1, R_2$ of $A$ to $F_M$ with residue maps onto $\bar F' =$ `Fbar` (the $q$-expansion function field over $\kappa$ at $\Gamma_N(p,M,H)$), $R_2$ being $\theta$-transported from $R_1$. Assume that for every $v \in F_{M/p}$ with $\alpha v$ integral for both, the $R_2$-residue of $\alpha v$ is the Frobenius `qExpFrobeniusModL` of its $R_1$-residue. Put $V := \alpha^{-1}(R_1.\text{integers})$, a valuation subring of $F_{M/p}$, and regard $F_M$ as a $V$-algebra through $\alpha$. Then for every $f \in F_M$ integral for both $R_1$ and $R_2$ and with both residues nonzero there is a finite subset $s \subseteq F_M$ such that each element of $s$ is integral over $V$, $f$ lies in the $V$-subalgebra $V[s]$ generated by $s$, the $F_{M/p}$-span of $s$ (via $\alpha$) is all of $F_M$, and for all $a, b \in \bar F'$ there is $g \in V[s]$, integral for both prolongations, with $R_1$-residue $a$ and $R_2$-residue $b$.
--
--   The statement produces the order $V[s]$ used as input to the norm computation for the two prolongations attached to $X_H(M)$ at $p$, in the valuation-theoretic form of the Kronecker congruence relation; the requirement that the two residue maps be jointly surjective on $V[s]$ encodes the independence of the two prolongations. It is cited in the derivation of the divisor and Frobenius relations for the model of $X_H(M)$ at $p$ ([`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_mapDomain_sp_eq_ord_and_ord_frob_eq_add_of_norm_of_prolongationDatum`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_mapDomain_sp_eq_ord_and_ord_frob_eq_add_of_norm_of_prolongationDatum)).
